
The C interpreter includes instruction sources generated by CLISP during the
build. Install CLISP, then run from the repository root:

    cmake -S . -B build
    cmake --build build --parallel

The generator writes the instruction sources into build/stub. These generated
files are not stored in the repository. Edit the Alpha assembler sources,
Lisp macros, or process.lisp to change the interpreter; CMake tracks these
dependencies and regenerates the C sources when needed.

The generate-stubs target runs just the generation step:

    cmake --build build --target generate-stubs

To run "clisp -norc process.lisp" directly from this directory, set
VLM_STUB_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY to an existing build directory with a trailing slash.
